    <h1>About LienForm</h1>

    <p class="lead">LienForm is a mechanics lien document generator for contractors, subcontractors, and material suppliers working on US construction projects.</p>

    <h2>What We Do</h2>
    <p>When a contractor or supplier doesn't get paid for work on a construction project, a mechanics lien attaches a legal claim to the property title — the owner can't sell or refinance until the debt is resolved.</p>
    <p>You enter your project details, and LienForm generates the complete set of documents pre-filled with your information and the correct statutory citation for your state.</p>

    <h2>Why We Built It</h2>
    <p>Most mechanics lien templates online cite outdated statutes. California's old §3082 was repealed in 2012 — competitors still cite it. Texas updated its monthly notice requirements via HB 2237 in 2022 — most templates don't reflect this. Michigan amended the Construction Lien Act in 2023 — old forms are wrong.</p>
    <p>LienForm tracks current law, correct citations, role-aware deadlines, and county-specific filing guidance for each state it supports.</p>

    <h2>What's Included in Every Bundle</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Mechanics Lien Claim with current statutory citation</li>
      <li>Deadline Confirmation — your exact filing deadline with days remaining</li>
      <li>County Recorder / Clerk Filing Instructions</li>
      <li>Proof of Service Affidavit</li>
      <li>Lien Release Form</li>
      <li>Preliminary Notice (auto-included for Michigan, California, and Florida subcontractors and suppliers, where required)</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>State Coverage</h2>
    <p>LienForm currently generates documents for Michigan, California, Texas, Arizona, Georgia, Ohio, Washington, and Florida (Notice to Owner). We're building out coverage for additional states.</p>
    <p>Each bundle is $24.99. Arizona's deadline depends on project completion rather than your last furnishing date, so that page shows a verification note instead of an automatic countdown — the document generator itself still works normally.</p>

    <h2>Important Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>LienForm is not a law firm and does not provide legal advice. Documents generated are for informational purposes only. Please consult a licensed attorney in your state before filing a lien.</p>

    <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
    <p>Questions or feedback? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
